---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import counterInputs from '../data/counter-inputs.json';

const BUILD_TS = Number(import.meta.env.BUILD_TIMESTAMP_MS) || Date.now();
const buildDateStr = new Date(BUILD_TS).toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace('T', ' ') + ' UTC';
---

<Base title="Methodology">
  <h1>Methodology</h1>

  <section>
    <h2>Counter Math</h2>
    <p>The live taxpayer-cost counter uses the following formula:</p>
    <pre class="formula-block"><code>referenceMs = Math.max(Date.now(), BUILD_TIMESTAMP)
elapsedMs   = Math.max(0, referenceMs - Date.parse(facilityOpenedAt))
total       = Math.floor(
                (oneTimeConstructionCostUSD ?? 0)
              + dailyOperatingCostUSD * (elapsedMs / 86_400_000)
              )</code></pre>
    <p>
      The counter ticks once per second (integer steps). Sub-second smoothing is intentionally
      omitted — real spending is stepwise and daily-aggregated; finer granularity would imply
      false precision.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Clock-skew guard:</strong> <code>BUILD_TIMESTAMP</code> is injected from
      <code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</code> at build time.
      <code>referenceMs = Math.max(Date.now(), BUILD_TIMESTAMP)</code> prevents wrong-clock
      devices from showing $0 or implausibly-future totals. The counter is monotonic
      non-decreasing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Current Inputs</h2>
    <table class="inputs-table">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Facility opened at</th>
          <td>{counterInputs.facilityOpenedAt ?? 'Not yet confirmed'}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">One-time construction cost</th>
          <td>
            {counterInputs.oneTimeConstructionCostUSD != null
              ? `$${counterInputs.oneTimeConstructionCostUSD.toLocaleString('en-US')}`
              : 'Not yet confirmed'}
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Daily operating cost</th>
          <td>
            {counterInputs.dailyOperatingCostUSD != null
              ? `$${counterInputs.dailyOperatingCostUSD.toLocaleString('en-US')}/day`
              : 'Not yet confirmed'}
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Confidence level</th>
          <td><code>{counterInputs.confidence}</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Last verified</th>
          <td>{counterInputs.lastVerified ?? 'N/A'}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Source IDs</th>
          <td>
            {counterInputs.inputsSourceIds.length > 0
              ? counterInputs.inputsSourceIds.map((id, i) => (
                  <>
                    {i > 0 && ', '}
                    <a href={`/sources#${id}`}>{id}</a>
                  </>
                ))
              : 'None yet'}
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Launch Gate</h2>
    <p>The live counter is only shown when the data meets a minimum evidence threshold:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Contracted</strong> — counter shown only if <code>inputsSourceIds</code> contains
        at least one source with <code>primarySource: true</code> (federal contract, state
        appropriation bill, official budget doc, or court filing).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reported estimate</strong> — counter shown only if <code>inputsSourceIds</code>
        contains at least one named-outlet citation (Miami Herald, AP, Reuters, NYT, WaPo,
        ProPublica, Tampa Bay Times, etc.) AND the UI visibly labels the figure
        "reported estimate."
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Projection</strong> — <em>not eligible</em> for the live counter; the
        pending-verification banner is shown instead.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If the gate is not met, the counter section is replaced by:
      <em>"Figures pending verification — site will update when primary sources confirm operating cost."</em>
    </p>
    <p>
      A manual kill switch (<code>PUBLIC_COUNTER_DISABLED=true</code> build-time env var) forces
      the banner regardless of gate status, for pausing the live tick within minutes if a figure
      is challenged post-launch.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Build Provenance</h2>
    <p>
      This build was generated on <strong>{buildDateStr}</strong>.
      <code>BUILD_TIMESTAMP_MS</code> is derived from
      <code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=$(git log -1 --format=%ct -- src/data/sources.json src/data/counter-inputs.json)</code>,
      giving a deterministic, reproducible build tied to the last data change.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
